  data: {
    LLM: "Try to play blocking dominoes early. Keep high-value dominoes (doubles) in hand as long as possible. Pay attention to which numbers have been played to know what tiles may be stuck in other players' hands. Always try to play blanks strategically on the cross to control the game.\n\nTrack opponent hands: Count remaining tiles and estimate their likely dominoes. Manage your own doubles carefullyâ€”holding unplayed doubles increases your penalty if you lose. Play defensively by blocking numbers opponents may need. Bluff by playing in patterns that suggest you have certain dominoes.\n\nPositional blocking: Play tiles that force opponents to draw multiple times, depleting the draw pile. Domino counting: Memorize all played dominoes to calculate exact probabilities of draws. Control the cross: By playing strategic dominoes on the center cross, limit the extensions available. Endgame calculation: When the game is nearly blocked, calculate whether finishing first or tying/blocking for lowest score is optimal.",
    Player: "Try to play blocking dominoes early. Keep high-value dominoes (doubles) in hand as long as possible. Pay attention to which numbers have been played to know what tiles may be stuck in other players' hands. Always try to play blanks strategically on the cross to control the game.\n\nTrack opponent hands: Count remaining tiles and estimate their likely dominoes. Manage your own doubles carefullyâ€”holding unplayed doubles increases your penalty if you lose. Play defensively by blocking numbers opponents may need. Bluff by playing in patterns that suggest you have certain dominoes.\n\nPositional blocking: Play tiles that force opponents to draw multiple times, depleting the draw pile. Domino counting: Memorize all played dominoes to calculate exact probabilities of draws. Control the cross: By playing strategic dominoes on the center cross, limit the extensions available. Endgame calculation: When the game is nearly blocked, calculate whether finishing first or tying/blocking for lowest score is optimal.",
